  <h3>Discord Mobile App: iOS vs Android</h3>
  <p>Small text renders differently between Discord's iOS and Android apps. <strong>iOS</strong> uses the San Francisco system font, which has broader Unicode coverage — Bubble Text and Bold render beautifully. <strong>Android</strong> devices vary by manufacturer; Samsung devices typically have the best Unicode support, while budget Android phones may display some characters as tofu (☐). Superscript text is the safest choice for mixed mobile channels.</p>
  <p>Quick test: if you see boxes instead of small text, that user is on a device with limited Unicode font coverage. There's nothing wrong with your text — the recipient's device simply lacks the required font glyphs.</p>
